<title>USA: CalEnergy says NYSEG antitrust wait expires.</title>
<headline>CalEnergy says NYSEG antitrust wait expires.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>CalEnergy Co Inc said the Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust waiting period regarding its $159 million tender offer for New York State Electric &amp; Gas Corp has expired.</p>
<p>CalEnergy has launched a hostile tender offer for 9.9 percent of NYSEG shares and said it intends to seek to acquire the rest of the company in a deal valued at $1.9 billion.</p>
<p>NYSEG last week rejected the offer.</p>
<p>The tender offer calls for the independent power producer to buy the stake for $24.50 per share. It has also offered to negotiate a friendly deal for $27.50 per share.</p>
<p>((--Robin Sidel, 212/859-1723))</p>
